  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to NRC Consortium under the Resilience and Adaptation Fund (RAF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will address critical challenges faced by both Rohingya refugees and host communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, related to climate vulnerability, environmental degradation, and limited livelihood opportunities. The project aims to build the resilience of the most vulnerable and food- and nutrition-insecure households to shocks and stresses particularly those driven by climate change.Youth will be trained in trades which are identified through NRC&#x2019;s youth-led market assessment. Graduates will receive tailored start-up kits, cash grants, job placements, and internships, complemented by mentoring and job fairs to facilitate sustainable income generation. Handicap International (HI) will ensure the inclusivity of consortium interventions by embedding disability-inclusive approaches across climate-resilient activities and empowering learners with disabilities by developing their skills to create income-generating opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
